{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles","id":1151602,"title":"Lancea Sanctum Domain titles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-21T01:59:28-07:00","id":1151602,"title":"Lancea Sanctum Domain titles","content":"I know that in Lancea Sanctum Domains their Prince is called Archbishop. <b>Is there a ready 'rewording' of typical positions in Domain to this Church Ethernal naming conventions?</b> In <b>Damnation City</b> there is mentiond of Synod as LS Elders council in city and Herold as personal servant to Archbishop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T07:13:07-07:00","id":1151635,"title":"","content":"Only if you want them. I used some titles from the Catholic Church but they didn't always correspond to the book description or serve as a complete vampire derivative to their human version. Or even have the same function in every setting.<br /> <br /> For instance, in one setting a ritemaster was the official Theban Sorcery expert. You needed their permission to teach or learn Theban Sorcery (or you may be paid a visit by the inquisitors). In another setting it was a Ventrue or Gangrel only position where they handled poisonous snakes (hemotoxic venom) for divination and initiation services.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T08:08:01-07:00","id":1151641,"title":"","content":"Who are those Inquisitors I read about here and there? Are they Lancea Sanctum variants of Sheriff general title?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T09:08:23-07:00","id":1151654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles?p=1151641#post1151641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are those Inquisitors I read about here and there? Are they Lancea Sanctum variants of Sheriff general title?</div> </div> </div> </div>There more internal to the Lancea Sanctum and try and keep the local orthodoxy but they can have further duties if the covenant controls the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T11:37:31-07:00","id":1151699,"title":"","content":"What Live Bait said. Generally I used them as covenant specific enforcers who levied punishments or fines for violation of Church regulations and doctrine. They occasionally avenged low status Sanctified members with a legitimate grievance against an Acolyte or Dragon when official city channels couldn't or wouldn't act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T12:26:39-07:00","id":1151708,"title":"","content":"The Bishop is the highest Lancea et Sanctum authority in a domain. If they are a Prince, they're an Archbishop. An Inquisitor is appointed 'to root out and destroy heresies within the parish.' But they're basically enforcers with a large variety of jobs. Priests serve as counselors to individual kindred and coteries. A Legate is someone who travels to other domains on behalf of their covenant. A Crusader, something not all domains will have, is more of an executioner or assassin.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of lay positions. You might check the Lancea et Sanctum book for specifics. That's where all this comes from.<br /> <br /> Some other terms for Archbishop used by the Lancea et Sanctum: Episkopos, Exarch, Father/Mother Superior. Bishops have Presbyter, Monsignor, and Shepherd. Priests have Pastor, Father/Mother, and Predicant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:23:50-07:00","id":1151726,"title":"","content":"So Inquisitor in Lancea Sanctum domain can easily be <i>de facto</i> local Sheriff, yes? But what would be his difference with Crusader of Lancea Sanctum then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:26:27-07:00","id":1151727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles?p=1151726#post1151726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Inquisitor in Lancea Sanctum domain can easily be <i>de facto</i> local Sheriff, yes? But what would be his difference with Crusader of Lancea Sanctum then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Inquisitor is basically a sheriff. But the sheriff investigates things, issues warnings and other things. They can be compared to secret police.<br /> <br /> Crusader is just there to fight and kill the enemies of the covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-21-2017, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:28:54-07:00","id":1151730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles?p=1151726#post1151726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Inquisitor in Lancea Sanctum domain can easily be <i>de facto</i> local Sheriff, yes? But what would be his difference with Crusader of Lancea Sanctum then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crusaders are external, think police Vs soldier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:30:11-07:00","id":1151731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles?p=1151727#post1151727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Inquisitor is basically a sheriff. But the sheriff investigates things, issues warnings and other things.<br /> <br /> Crusader is just there to fight and kill the enemies of the covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Crusaders are what generally is called Hounds in domains? Typical enforcers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:48:00-07:00","id":1151739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles?p=1151731#post1151731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Crusaders are what generally is called Hounds in domains? Typical enforcers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the entirety of their brief section. Covenants: the Lancea Sanctum, p72.<br /> <br /> 'Similar in more secular parlance to a medieval knight, a Crusader is not a leader among the Sanctified, nor is he a mere soldier. The Crusaders are also not considered Inquisitors. More or less, a Crusader is a member of the 'elite' warriors of the Lancea Sanctum. Renowned for their martial ability, they are fierce combatants, feared assassins, and cold killers. Crusaders are perhaps overly indoctrinated into the covenant, set upon rigid schedules of prayer and ritae, nigh fanatically enthusiastic to do anything (including meet Final Death) for the covenant. Crusaders are also expected to keep up their martial training (and this can include any kind of fighting, be it with melee weapons, firearms, or abstract tactics). They are not viewed as individual Kindred. They are seen as predatory weapons meant to be wielded for the glory and grace of the Dark Prophet. Many Sanctified see this position as outdated and bullish, though other older Sanctified feel that when the time comes, they\u2019d rather have the protection than be without it.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T17:17:47-07:00","id":1151794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles?p=1151731#post1151731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Crusaders are what generally is called Hounds in domains? Typical enforcers?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have a default domain setting analog. If you're sticking with the police analogy, an inquisitor would be a police detective who turns off the recorders and beats the crap out of you in the interrogation room. A crusader would be a SWAT team member who takes the headshot to kill the suspect while the negotiator is talking. If you're going Catholic counterparts, inquisitors are Jesuits, crusaders are Knights Templar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T17:59:23-08:00","id":1158303,"title":"","content":"In my New York City setting (the Night Cities), each of the Boroughs has a Prince and maintains their own court and laws. In theory they are all subservient to the Prince of Manhattan.<br /> <br /> Since 2000, Manhattan has been controlled by a Sanctified who goes by the title &quot;Prince-Archbishop.&quot;<br /> <br /> Below him, he has a Primogeon made up of Kindred from each of the Covenants. He also has a Synod made up of the leaders of the Sanctified across all of the Night Cities: this includes parish priests and Bishops. <br /> <br /> His Seneschal is from the Invictus.<br /> <br /> His Sheriff is called the Grand Inquisitor, and her Hounds are called Inquisitors.<br /> <br /> Otherwise most of the other positions are held by a variety of Invictus and Sanctified without the need for special titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T08:17:31-08:00","id":1158477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umoja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1151602-lancea-sanctum-domain-titles?p=1158303#post1158303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His Seneschal is from the Invictus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lay-Bishop would be an interesting title for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T05:25:08-08:00","id":1159791,"title":"","content":"As far as I know the leader of the Lancea Sanctum is a Bishop, if a member of the Lancea Sanctum is a Prince, he'd be referred to as an Archbishop, if he's both the highest authority in the Lancea Sanctum AND a Prince, he'd be called a Cardinal. Then again he could simply call himself Prince, like the case of Augusto Vidal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}